1
00:01:56,253 --> 00:02:04,003
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:04,070 --> 00:02:08,340
No living creature was harmed
during the filming.

3
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:11,260
Mother, you are wounded!
Who did this?

4
00:02:11,260 --> 00:02:13,510
Wait, son.
I'm not wounded.

5
00:02:14,670 --> 00:02:16,530
But, Cornelia...

6
00:02:17,045 --> 00:02:19,795
he wounded her and escaped.

7
00:02:22,020 --> 00:02:23,970
Go to the tent at once.

8
00:02:23,970 --> 00:02:25,040
Come on, Bala!

9
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:27,370
What are you saying?

10
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:31,270
His face was covered.
I couldn't see.

11
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:37,220
They enter my mother's tent?

12
00:02:38,570 --> 00:02:42,040
What are you doing here?
Find him!

13
00:02:42,170 --> 00:02:44,440
My bey, I sent the alps.

14
00:02:44,570 --> 00:02:46,110
They are searching everywhere.

15
00:02:46,110 --> 00:02:47,520
We'll find him.

16
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:50,840
Are you alright?

17
00:02:51,740 --> 00:02:54,770
That dog tried to kill me, son.

18
00:02:54,990 --> 00:02:56,520
Mother.

19
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:01,620
Mother.

20
00:03:03,670 --> 00:03:05,870
Tell me all about it.

21
00:03:14,670 --> 00:03:15,870
Mother Selcan!

22
00:03:20,170 --> 00:03:22,840
Who are you?

23
00:03:30,720 --> 00:03:31,820
Alps!

24
00:03:31,990 --> 00:03:33,720
Alps! Help!

25
00:03:34,990 --> 00:03:36,790
Alps!

26
00:03:37,170 --> 00:03:37,990
Mother!

27
00:03:38,240 --> 00:03:39,070
What's happening?

28
00:03:39,140 --> 00:03:41,284
He is running away!

29
00:03:41,470 --> 00:03:42,220
Alps!

30
00:03:42,370 --> 00:03:43,440
Catch him!

31
00:03:43,570 --> 00:03:45,420
Hang on, my girl.

32
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:54,170
He stormed in and stormed out.

33
00:03:54,590 --> 00:03:56,140
He knew the place.

34
00:03:56,770 --> 00:03:57,870
It's apparent.

35
00:03:58,370 --> 00:04:00,340
It's one of us, son.

36
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:07,270
Osman Bey.

37
00:04:07,690 --> 00:04:10,040
Selcan Hatun is right.

38
00:04:12,290 --> 00:04:16,839
That snake infiltrated the tribe.

39
00:04:18,740 --> 00:04:20,589
Alps are searching.

40
00:04:21,339 --> 00:04:22,820
He'll be found.

41
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:29,220
Many traitors stood behind us.

42
00:04:31,140 --> 00:04:33,340
They looked into our eyes...

43
00:04:37,390 --> 00:04:41,570
but we always waited for
the right time.

44
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:51,540
He'll be found.

45
00:04:57,590 --> 00:05:00,440
Thank Allah.
Selcan Hatun is safe.

46
00:05:01,640 --> 00:05:04,090
Let's leave her to rest.

47
00:05:04,770 --> 00:05:06,040
If you allow us.

48
00:05:06,078 --> 00:05:07,192
Thank Allah.

49
00:05:07,690 --> 00:05:09,490
It's late, İbrahim Fakih.

50
00:05:09,820 --> 00:05:11,740
Stay in the tribe tonight.

51
00:05:12,140 --> 00:05:13,320
Do you allow it, my bey?

52
00:05:31,090 --> 00:05:32,940
Slowly.

53
00:05:41,640 --> 00:05:42,790
Cornelia.

54
00:05:42,970 --> 00:05:44,490
How did it happen?

55
00:05:44,520 --> 00:05:46,570
Where were you?
How did you notice it?

56
00:05:46,620 --> 00:05:49,170
Mother Selcan was performing
prayer.

57
00:05:49,390 --> 00:05:51,270
And I was laying there.

58
00:05:51,920 --> 00:05:53,790
Someone entered.

59
00:05:54,340 --> 00:05:57,190
Did you wound him?

60
00:05:57,570 --> 00:06:01,020
No. I didn't have a sword
or a dagger.

61
00:06:02,020 --> 00:06:03,640
I jumped him.

62
00:06:03,940 --> 00:06:06,190
I couldn't think of anything
else.

63
00:06:17,570 --> 00:06:20,240
We should go now.
Take some rest.

64
00:06:20,540 --> 00:06:22,340
Thank you, Cornelia.

65
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:33,040
Good night.

66
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:35,040
Keep your eyes on her.

67
00:06:52,320 --> 00:06:53,630
You weren't spotted, right?

68
00:06:53,630 --> 00:06:54,440
No, my bey.

69
00:06:54,740 --> 00:06:56,170
No one saw me.

70
00:06:56,420 --> 00:06:58,490
The old woman couldn't
describe you either.

71
00:06:58,620 --> 00:06:59,820
You hid yourself well.

72
00:06:59,990 --> 00:07:00,990
Well done.

73
00:07:01,820 --> 00:07:03,320
Thank you, my bey.

74
00:07:03,570 --> 00:07:05,370
I did it easily.

75
00:07:05,870 --> 00:07:08,040
They know that it's someone
from inside.

76
00:07:08,940 --> 00:07:10,520
You will be cautious.

77
00:07:16,590 --> 00:07:19,340
You are in a dark corridor, Osman.

78
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:23,920
You are blind.

79
00:07:25,170 --> 00:07:28,820
Your suspicions are all cut
by me.

80
00:07:30,490 --> 00:07:34,040
Selcan Hatun and Osman will
trust Cornelia.

81
00:07:38,340 --> 00:07:39,240
My bey.

82
00:07:39,940 --> 00:07:41,590
He ran away.

83
00:07:42,290 --> 00:07:43,720
We closed the tribe.

84
00:07:44,020 --> 00:07:45,420
We'll interrogate everyone.

85
00:07:45,420 --> 00:07:47,390
We'll search the surrounding.

86
00:07:48,270 --> 00:07:50,390
How can you let him go?

87
00:07:50,840 --> 00:07:52,620
How can you?

88
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:55,170
My bey, I was chasing him.

89
00:07:55,290 --> 00:07:57,140
He dissappeared.

90
00:07:58,440 --> 00:08:00,570
Interrogate all the alps.

91
00:08:01,020 --> 00:08:02,070
All of them!

92
00:08:02,170 --> 00:08:03,920
The traitor is still
in the tribe.

93
00:08:14,990 --> 00:08:16,720
Have you found anything.

94
00:08:17,140 --> 00:08:18,870
We found this in my mother's
tent.

95
00:08:18,870 --> 00:08:19,990
It belongs to Cornelia.

96
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:29,320
It seems like she hid the
poison there, my bey.

97
00:08:33,219 --> 00:08:35,070
You were right, mother.

98
00:08:37,140 --> 00:08:39,240
We blamed Zehra for nothing.

99
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:44,520
The snake was carrying the poison
on her neck.

100
00:08:46,270 --> 00:08:47,820
What about today?

101
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:50,990
Have you learned anything?

102
00:08:54,140 --> 00:08:56,290
But he is suspicious of you, Barkın.

103
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:59,080
He thinks the Mongols didn't kill Umur.

104
00:08:59,270 --> 00:09:00,890
What does he have?

105
00:09:01,390 --> 00:09:02,970
He can test me.

106
00:09:03,730 --> 00:09:06,790
Because I ruined his power structure.

107
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:09,780
He looks for a weak spot.

108
00:09:09,790 --> 00:09:10,590
Don't.

109
00:09:10,870 --> 00:09:12,640
Don't, Barkın.

110
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:14,720
Don't underestimate him.

111
00:09:15,420 --> 00:09:19,220
The one who underestimate his enemy
is destined to be destroyed.

112
00:09:21,220 --> 00:09:22,370
What will we do?

113
00:09:22,470 --> 00:09:24,020
Barkın Bey, may I enter?

114
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:25,320
Come in.

115
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:30,290
Barkın Bey.
İbrahim Fakih.

116
00:09:30,720 --> 00:09:32,670
Osman Bey summons you.

117
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:39,820
What if he found us?

118
00:09:40,670 --> 00:09:41,890
What will we do?

119
00:09:42,440 --> 00:09:46,140
We'll clear all his suspicions.

120
00:09:53,690 --> 00:09:57,140
She says that she didn't
have a weapon but...

121
00:09:57,490 --> 00:09:59,820
she hides a dagger under
her pillow.

122
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:02,530
She didn't even touch
the dagger.

123
00:10:02,690 --> 00:10:05,470
Wouldn't one run to their weapon
in such a state of fear?

124
00:10:08,790 --> 00:10:11,770
Cornelia's treachery is obvious.

125
00:10:13,170 --> 00:10:15,340
She poisoned herself.

126
00:10:15,970 --> 00:10:20,890
Then, she made a new plan
after seeing my doubts.

127
00:10:21,970 --> 00:10:24,840
She saved me from the enemy.

128
00:10:26,690 --> 00:10:28,620
And became a hero, huh?

129
00:10:28,820 --> 00:10:30,690
She couldn't do it all alone.

130
00:10:31,070 --> 00:10:32,690
Mari's death.

131
00:10:32,690 --> 00:10:34,740
Explosion at Söğüt.

132
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:38,740
Are they all related, my bey?

133
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:40,290
Not Cornelia.

134
00:10:40,740 --> 00:10:42,090
She is a tool.

135
00:10:43,220 --> 00:10:45,470
We need the one holding it.

136
00:10:47,140 --> 00:10:48,770
But...

137
00:10:50,770 --> 00:10:52,840
I'm suspicious of Barkın and Selvi.

138
00:10:52,970 --> 00:10:57,320
They made a fait accompli with the
beyhood elections.

139
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:03,590
I thought of that.

140
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:08,270
What connection might they have
to Cornelia.

141
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:12,420
You'll figure it out, mother.

142
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:15,740
You'll make Cornelia speak.

143
00:11:16,690 --> 00:11:18,240
My bey, allow me.

144
00:11:18,790 --> 00:11:20,290
I'll make her speak.

145
00:11:20,920 --> 00:11:24,270
If you scare the scorpion,
it'll poison itself.

146
00:11:26,190 --> 00:11:28,120
We won't scare her.

147
00:11:29,940 --> 00:11:32,420
As they killed Mari Hatun...

148
00:11:33,440 --> 00:11:35,640
she will be punished.

149
00:11:38,890 --> 00:11:40,490
An eye for an eye.

150
00:11:41,470 --> 00:11:43,790
Don't worry, son.

151
00:11:44,770 --> 00:11:48,190
For the pain she made Mari
suffer...

152
00:11:48,770 --> 00:11:51,840
she'll pay severely.

153
00:11:52,070 --> 00:11:53,740
Indeed.

154
00:11:59,590 --> 00:12:02,620
Harmankaya Castle

155
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:23,720
You thought so long, Turgut Bey.

156
00:12:24,290 --> 00:12:27,720
In the end, you are a man of the steppes.

157
00:12:27,840 --> 00:12:29,870
What will you do with
the castle?

158
00:12:30,220 --> 00:12:32,870
A castle is a cage for you.

159
00:12:33,140 --> 00:12:36,120
But spoils? It isn't.

160
00:12:46,190 --> 00:12:47,320
Gold.

161
00:12:49,590 --> 00:12:50,740
It's good.

162
00:12:54,220 --> 00:12:55,840
But not enough.

163
00:12:56,420 --> 00:12:57,830
I'll enter your market...

164
00:12:59,340 --> 00:13:00,840
and sell my goods.

165
00:13:01,590 --> 00:13:05,140
But I won't give you a single coin.

166
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:10,590
Alright, you won't pay a single coin.

167
00:13:10,740 --> 00:13:13,440
I'll pay you a tribute.

168
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:17,690
But the castle is mine.

169
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:23,620
It doesn't fit a bey to make a decision
without the council.

170
00:13:24,690 --> 00:13:28,190
I want to hear what my alps
and beys want to say.

171
00:13:29,890 --> 00:13:34,890
Osman is talking about conquest. I don't
want my alps to follow him.

172
00:13:35,020 --> 00:13:36,420
You wouldn't want that.

173
00:13:38,240 --> 00:13:39,720
Alright.

174
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:42,820
Alright.

175
00:13:44,440 --> 00:13:48,190
I rather wait than see Osman stronger.

176
00:13:49,270 --> 00:13:51,620
Osman is already strong.

177
00:13:52,340 --> 00:13:54,820
When he hears that you
took İnhisar...

178
00:13:55,160 --> 00:13:59,340
he'll come at both of
your castles.

179
00:13:59,690 --> 00:14:01,670
It won't happen.

180
00:14:01,790 --> 00:14:03,520
If it does...

181
00:14:03,590 --> 00:14:06,390
he'll face the consequences.

182
00:14:08,570 --> 00:14:09,890
I think...

183
00:14:10,670 --> 00:14:14,820
still, don't underestimate him, Nikola.

184
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:17,720
Don't underestimate him, Nikola.

185
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:20,870
We take gold as spoils.

186
00:14:20,970 --> 00:14:24,140
Osman took hundreds of Fyling Flame
barrels from Geyhatu.

187
00:14:24,140 --> 00:14:25,240
He has it all.

188
00:14:25,590 --> 00:14:27,220
He didn't give us any.

189
00:14:29,380 --> 00:14:37,190
If he comes at you with all of them,
it will be hell.

190
00:14:37,640 --> 00:14:40,620
He doesn't have the Flying Flame anymore.

191
00:14:47,590 --> 00:14:50,640
Without them...

192
00:14:51,540 --> 00:14:54,020
Osman can't do anything.

193
00:14:55,470 --> 00:15:00,770
And, how can you be so sure?

194
00:15:01,170 --> 00:15:02,890
It's Osman, Kosses.

195
00:15:02,970 --> 00:15:05,040
Is it possible to be sure?

196
00:15:05,940 --> 00:15:09,970
But if he had the Flying Flame...

197
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:13,390
he would use it.

198
00:15:13,590 --> 00:15:15,590
Right?

199
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:17,570
Right?

200
00:15:18,290 --> 00:15:19,570
Right?

201
00:15:22,220 --> 00:15:23,340
Anyway.

202
00:15:23,670 --> 00:15:25,270
I have business.

203
00:15:25,520 --> 00:15:26,870
Until next time.

204
00:15:27,020 --> 00:15:28,220
Farewell.

205
00:15:37,890 --> 00:15:40,140
Nikola is involved.

206
00:15:40,290 --> 00:15:42,190
Dishonorable.

207
00:15:44,110 --> 00:15:45,100
But this time...

208
00:15:45,120 --> 00:15:47,140
he won't be saved.

209
00:15:49,570 --> 00:15:50,490
Right?

210
00:15:59,290 --> 00:16:01,570
Oh, Mari the Pretty.

211
00:16:02,190 --> 00:16:05,790
She past away before seeing
her child because of her.

212
00:16:06,640 --> 00:16:12,240
Wouldn't I rip her into pieces for
killing an innocent?

213
00:16:13,540 --> 00:16:16,090
Cornelia hurt many, mother.

214
00:16:16,790 --> 00:16:18,940
She was about to make brothers
kill brothers.

215
00:16:19,090 --> 00:16:21,240
She hurt many poor people.

216
00:16:21,570 --> 00:16:23,240
No punishment is enough.

217
00:16:25,240 --> 00:16:28,590
An enemy faces you and draws
his weapon.

218
00:16:29,520 --> 00:16:33,190
Snakes like her crawl into
you sneakily.

219
00:16:33,870 --> 00:16:36,640
They don't deserve an honorable death.

220
00:16:37,970 --> 00:16:40,770
Scorpions, centipedes...

221
00:16:40,990 --> 00:16:42,920
but if I'm Selcan...

222
00:16:43,220 --> 00:16:49,290
I'll dry her blood out!

223
00:17:19,770 --> 00:17:21,490
May I enter, my bey.

224
00:17:22,819 --> 00:17:24,190
Come in.

225
00:17:48,790 --> 00:17:51,190
Do you know why I summoned you?

226
00:17:54,170 --> 00:17:57,420
Beys have many mysteries, Osman Bey.

227
00:17:57,670 --> 00:18:00,340
It's apparent that what you have
to say is important.

228
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:02,690
It's important.

229
00:18:04,340 --> 00:18:05,940
Of course, it is.

230
00:18:15,840 --> 00:18:18,070
The ones who attacked my mother...

231
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:22,540
and the ones who attacked my sheik
are the same people.

232
00:18:27,340 --> 00:18:30,590
So are the ones who killed Umur Bey
and İhvaz Bey.

233
00:18:38,490 --> 00:18:40,340
Their purpose...

234
00:18:44,090 --> 00:18:47,120
is to demolish the mountains
I lay my back on.

235
00:18:47,490 --> 00:18:48,790
I don't know the others.

236
00:18:49,690 --> 00:18:52,920
But it was Mongols who killed
Umur Bey, my bey.

237
00:18:57,940 --> 00:18:59,940
It's not the Mongols.

238
00:19:05,690 --> 00:19:07,470
It's someone else.

239
00:19:07,790 --> 00:19:09,870
I fought the Mongols.

240
00:19:10,920 --> 00:19:12,790
Mongols killed Umur Bey.

241
00:19:14,290 --> 00:19:17,210
Speak openly about what you
are suspicious of, Osman Bey.

242
00:19:21,190 --> 00:19:22,520
Barkın Bey.

243
00:19:23,840 --> 00:19:28,240
I've seen demons in disguise of
statesman, scholar, and warrior.

244
00:19:30,240 --> 00:19:33,820
Many were good at hiding.

245
00:19:35,190 --> 00:19:37,170
You can't make a decision over
suspicions.

246
00:19:40,170 --> 00:19:46,140
The demon makes you know,
whatever he wants you to know.

247
00:19:50,640 --> 00:19:53,090
Who is in your mind, Osman Bey?

248
00:19:55,470 --> 00:19:57,170
Who are you suspicious of?

249
00:20:13,470 --> 00:20:14,990
Nikola.

250
00:20:20,140 --> 00:20:21,890
It's his style.

251
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:25,370
But...

252
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:28,720
we'll make sure.

253
00:20:29,970 --> 00:20:32,920
We can't act as Geyhatu says.

254
00:20:35,920 --> 00:20:39,020
I'll go to where Umur Bey passed away.

255
00:21:04,870 --> 00:21:07,870
You won't doubt me now, Selcan.

256
00:21:09,740 --> 00:21:13,490
I'll make you suffer one day.

257
00:21:25,770 --> 00:21:29,270
Cornelia, my beautiful girl.

258
00:21:32,040 --> 00:21:33,620
Mother Selcan.

259
00:21:35,620 --> 00:21:37,820
Oh, my beautiful girl.

260
00:21:38,490 --> 00:21:41,120
My brave girl.

261
00:21:41,840 --> 00:21:46,640
You risked your life to
save mine.

262
00:21:47,190 --> 00:21:50,370
Now, you are my daughter.

263
00:21:53,170 --> 00:21:55,770
You are precious to me too,
Mother Selcan.

264
00:21:59,520 --> 00:22:03,940
I made it for you with my
own hands.

265
00:22:19,340 --> 00:22:21,640
To heal you.

266
00:22:23,470 --> 00:22:26,290
to get you on your feet in no time.

267
00:22:30,770 --> 00:22:34,040
To make you pay for the blood spilled.

268
00:22:37,120 --> 00:22:39,420
It's so delicious!

269
00:22:39,820 --> 00:22:42,120
Enjoy it, my beautiful girl.

270
00:22:42,340 --> 00:22:44,420
Let it be a cure for you.

271
00:22:53,870 --> 00:22:58,920
I'll see the corpses of the Mongol
warriors killed by Barkın and the field.

272
00:23:02,090 --> 00:23:06,370
Whoever this enemy is,
in Mongol disguise...

273
00:23:07,390 --> 00:23:09,120
but is something else.

274
00:23:11,120 --> 00:23:12,590
Alright, my bey.

275
00:23:13,990 --> 00:23:17,870
Let it be your way, then.

276
00:23:19,540 --> 00:23:21,890
Tomorrow, the truth will be revealed.

277
00:23:23,290 --> 00:23:25,870
We'll find out the truth.

278
00:23:30,840 --> 00:23:32,290
You are allowed to leave.

279
00:23:33,940 --> 00:23:36,570
May Allah help you, Osman Bey.

280
00:23:56,440 --> 00:23:58,490
My bey, may I enter.

281
00:23:59,840 --> 00:24:01,140
Come in.

282
00:24:07,870 --> 00:24:11,270
News from Turgut Bey and
Kosses, my bey.

283
00:24:11,820 --> 00:24:16,590
Whoever the enemy is, they say that
Nikola is with him.

284
00:24:16,890 --> 00:24:18,590
Let them know, then.

285
00:24:19,290 --> 00:24:21,390
They should release the bird
in the cage.

286
00:24:24,340 --> 00:24:26,420
He should tell everything
to Nikola.

287
00:24:27,970 --> 00:24:29,190
As you order, my bey.

288
00:24:35,070 --> 00:24:37,770
İnhisar Castle

289
00:24:54,120 --> 00:24:57,520
-Commander Antonio!
-I wouldn't let you stay here.

290
00:25:02,170 --> 00:25:04,220
God bless you, Commander Niko.

291
00:25:07,390 --> 00:25:10,190
The secret passage is open, sir.

292
00:25:10,450 --> 00:25:14,140
If you want to take revenge, Osman and
the others will be at Kurt Strait.

293
00:25:15,070 --> 00:25:16,170
Let's go, sir.

294
00:25:30,670 --> 00:25:31,820
Get up.

295
00:25:38,370 --> 00:25:40,120
He took the bait.

296
00:25:48,620 --> 00:25:51,570
I knew it from the
beginning...

297
00:25:51,740 --> 00:25:56,190
that dishonorable Nikola had a part
in Mari's death.

298
00:25:56,370 --> 00:25:58,870
We knew it.
Now we are sure of it.

299
00:26:01,040 --> 00:26:02,770
Now is the time to settle it.

300
00:26:02,920 --> 00:26:05,640
Matheus will tell Nikola about
our location.

301
00:26:07,470 --> 00:26:09,270
My only wish from God is...

302
00:26:09,690 --> 00:26:14,140
to have that masked weasel,
who caused everything, be there.

303
00:26:14,370 --> 00:26:17,170
They aren't brave enough to fight alone.

304
00:26:17,890 --> 00:26:19,820
That dog will be there.

305
00:26:20,640 --> 00:26:21,820
He should.

306
00:26:22,670 --> 00:26:24,620
So that we can end it.

307
00:26:32,320 --> 00:26:34,090
The gone won't come back.

308
00:26:34,620 --> 00:26:35,390
I know it.

309
00:26:36,340 --> 00:26:40,440
But the responsible will die today.

310
00:26:49,370 --> 00:26:50,770
Kutay is coming.

311
00:26:54,890 --> 00:26:56,220
Speak, Kutay.

312
00:26:57,920 --> 00:26:59,870
My bey. They are coming.

313
00:27:03,170 --> 00:27:04,870
It's time, Kosses.

314
00:27:05,940 --> 00:27:07,540
We are moving!

315
00:28:05,400 --> 00:28:08,290
İnegöl Castle

316
00:28:23,890 --> 00:28:25,970
Argus, report!

317
00:28:26,290 --> 00:28:29,140
The passages are closed, sir.
The walls are strengthened.

318
00:28:29,670 --> 00:28:32,590
-We took cautions for entrances.
-Good!

319
00:28:33,490 --> 00:28:35,990
Is this what you are strengthening the
castle with?

320
00:28:35,990 --> 00:28:37,770
Good. Good.

321
00:28:39,190 --> 00:28:41,040
I have only one wish.

322
00:28:41,420 --> 00:28:44,220
İnegöl! This stone castle...

323
00:28:44,690 --> 00:28:47,670
will be a stone grave for those
who wish to take it.

324
00:28:48,070 --> 00:28:50,020
Don't worry, sir.

325
00:28:51,890 --> 00:28:54,120
-What about the ditches?
-Ready, sir.

326
00:28:54,340 --> 00:28:56,120
-Good.
-Sir!

327
00:28:57,670 --> 00:29:00,290
Lord of İnhisar, Matheus is here.

328
00:29:20,570 --> 00:29:22,790
Turgut took your castle.

329
00:29:23,820 --> 00:29:26,070
And you came here.

330
00:29:27,470 --> 00:29:28,970
Is that so?

331
00:29:29,520 --> 00:29:31,420
I wonder why, Nikola!

332
00:29:32,420 --> 00:29:35,110
You didn't come to the dinner that
you said you would.

333
00:29:35,240 --> 00:29:37,590
Turgut didn't take my castle alone.

334
00:29:38,390 --> 00:29:40,790
Turgut, Kosses, and Osman!

335
00:29:41,870 --> 00:29:43,390
Osman?

336
00:29:45,390 --> 00:29:46,990
Idiots!

337
00:29:47,720 --> 00:29:51,120
Idiots... Idiot Kosses!

338
00:29:51,220 --> 00:29:53,120
Idiot Turgut!

339
00:29:53,120 --> 00:29:56,220
They wandered around...

340
00:29:56,220 --> 00:29:59,370
and worked with Osman again!

341
00:30:00,840 --> 00:30:05,140
They are loyal like dogs!

342
00:30:08,770 --> 00:30:12,620
Then, Gündüz...

343
00:30:13,770 --> 00:30:16,370
Gündüz didn't die...

344
00:30:17,890 --> 00:30:20,120
Osman...

345
00:30:22,320 --> 00:30:26,170
My soldier said that Osman
will be at Kurt Strait.

346
00:30:27,190 --> 00:30:29,490
Let's finish it, Nikola.

347
00:30:35,120 --> 00:30:38,120
I will, Matheus.

348
00:30:41,940 --> 00:30:43,740
I will.

349
00:31:05,390 --> 00:31:07,520
Mother Selcan.

350
00:31:09,040 --> 00:31:10,390
Mother Selcan.

351
00:31:11,670 --> 00:31:13,170
I don't feel good.

352
00:31:14,670 --> 00:31:16,890
I'm in great pain!

353
00:31:17,020 --> 00:31:20,170
What is it, my girl?
What's wrong.

354
00:31:26,070 --> 00:31:28,420
My stomach...
My stomach.

355
00:31:28,920 --> 00:31:33,090
Allah Allah! Is it something
you ate?

356
00:31:35,390 --> 00:31:36,790
Oh, oh...

357
00:31:37,620 --> 00:31:39,770
I remembered Mari now.

358
00:31:40,770 --> 00:31:44,190
She was in pain, just like you.

359
00:31:49,620 --> 00:31:51,160
Oh, Cornelia?

360
00:31:51,320 --> 00:31:54,490
Were you poisoned, my girl?

361
00:31:56,640 --> 00:31:58,740
You drank sherbet.

362
00:32:04,640 --> 00:32:08,820
Were you poisoned, my girl?

363
00:32:32,440 --> 00:32:35,590
So, this is where they attacked, Barkın?

364
00:32:37,790 --> 00:32:40,040
We attacked, Osman Bey.

365
00:32:44,170 --> 00:32:45,720
We attacked.

366
00:32:46,440 --> 00:32:47,990
Umur Bey ordered us.

367
00:32:47,990 --> 00:32:49,680
And we charged.

368
00:32:49,990 --> 00:32:51,990
But it was an ambush.

369
00:32:53,740 --> 00:32:55,240
True.

370
00:32:56,940 --> 00:32:58,590
You were ambushed.

371
00:33:03,190 --> 00:33:06,920
Alps. Boran. Cerkutay.

372
00:33:07,240 --> 00:33:08,640
Check around.

373
00:33:09,190 --> 00:33:12,170
See where they attacked from.

374
00:33:12,170 --> 00:33:14,170
As you order, my bey.

375
00:33:30,190 --> 00:33:32,540
Tell me, Barkın.

376
00:33:36,740 --> 00:33:38,620
Where did the arrow come from?

377
00:33:39,940 --> 00:33:41,620
Where did Umur Bey fall?

378
00:33:42,540 --> 00:33:44,740
Where did they come from?

379
00:33:46,570 --> 00:33:49,620
How did it happen?

380
00:33:51,470 --> 00:33:53,770
We followed them this way.

381
00:33:53,770 --> 00:33:55,770
But they lured us into a trap.

382
00:33:56,920 --> 00:33:59,920
They first attacked here.

383
00:34:00,690 --> 00:34:03,490
They charged at us from all
sides.

384
00:34:03,490 --> 00:34:05,490
And we fought.

385
00:34:11,370 --> 00:34:13,020
Brother.

386
00:34:17,489 --> 00:34:18,489
My bey.

387
00:34:20,040 --> 00:34:21,969
There are dry blood marks.

388
00:34:30,070 --> 00:34:31,469
Alps.

389
00:34:33,370 --> 00:34:34,840
Be cautious.

390
00:34:55,550 --> 00:34:57,540
Söğüt

391
00:35:06,340 --> 00:35:09,470
Selcan stopped me from seeing
Cornelia.

392
00:35:10,620 --> 00:35:12,270
She just said that she is fine.

393
00:35:24,940 --> 00:35:27,670
Something is happening in the tribe,
Ishak.

394
00:35:33,270 --> 00:35:35,190
I need to talk to Cornelia.

395
00:36:45,770 --> 00:36:48,220
Our companion will amuse him
for a while.

396
00:36:48,220 --> 00:36:50,220
Osman wants to be our shadow.

397
00:36:50,420 --> 00:36:53,090
But the darkness has no shadow.

398
00:36:53,320 --> 00:36:56,260
We need to catch up with our
soldiers. There will be blood.

399
00:36:57,090 --> 00:37:03,540
My girl. Let me tell you.
You must be poisoned.

400
00:37:03,540 --> 00:37:07,670
Mari was suffering just like you.

401
00:37:07,670 --> 00:37:11,690
Oh my!
You drank sherbet.

402
00:37:12,870 --> 00:37:15,240
Yes. Surely!

403
00:37:16,370 --> 00:37:18,840
There is a scorpion in
the tribe.

404
00:37:18,840 --> 00:37:23,220
It keeps poisoning the innocent.
How couldn't I think that?

405
00:37:25,390 --> 00:37:26,540
I don't understand it?

406
00:37:27,120 --> 00:37:29,890
Why would anyone poison me, Mother Selcan?

407
00:37:32,570 --> 00:37:34,390
You are right, my girl.

408
00:37:35,540 --> 00:37:37,320
You are right.

409
00:37:37,320 --> 00:37:40,970
Is there any other snake
than you to do that?

410
00:37:43,170 --> 00:37:44,240
Yes.

411
00:37:44,240 --> 00:37:46,840
You will look at me like this.

412
00:37:48,740 --> 00:37:52,270
If you are a demon, I'm Selcan!

413
00:37:53,490 --> 00:37:57,970
I wasn't born yesterday!

414
00:37:57,970 --> 00:38:00,940
Look! That's how I poisoned you.

415
00:38:02,870 --> 00:38:05,290
But my poison is nothing
like yours.

416
00:38:05,390 --> 00:38:11,720
I'll make you regret everything!

417
00:39:04,640 --> 00:39:05,820
My bey.

418
00:39:09,420 --> 00:39:10,820
Arrow mark.

419
00:39:30,240 --> 00:39:35,070
Is it a Mongol arrow?

420
00:39:36,820 --> 00:39:38,670
Brother.

421
00:39:46,220 --> 00:39:48,340
It isn't ours.

422
00:40:06,420 --> 00:40:08,940
The lord has ours.

423
00:40:10,820 --> 00:40:12,840
This is a Mongol arrow.

424
00:40:18,120 --> 00:40:20,390
Have you found anything, Osman Bey?

425
00:40:39,290 --> 00:40:40,540
Osman Bey.

426
00:41:09,640 --> 00:41:11,120
Keep searching.

427
00:41:14,740 --> 00:41:16,290
Alright, Osman Bey.

428
00:41:54,590 --> 00:41:56,690
Barkın is aware.

429
00:41:56,690 --> 00:41:58,690
Of what, sir?

430
00:41:59,490 --> 00:42:01,970
That we aren't setting the
trap here.

431
00:42:03,840 --> 00:42:05,520
Look, İshak.

432
00:42:06,920 --> 00:42:09,390
Would you come to a suspicious
place...

433
00:42:09,590 --> 00:42:11,890
with so little of an army?

434
00:42:20,940 --> 00:42:23,370
Osman knew that we would
come here.

435
00:42:23,640 --> 00:42:25,970
He knows that we'll attack him.

436
00:42:26,540 --> 00:42:31,170
I'm sure that he has cavalry waiting
to destroy us.

437
00:42:43,970 --> 00:42:45,720
Come on.

438
00:42:49,190 --> 00:42:50,940
Soon, Turgut.

439
00:42:51,640 --> 00:42:55,270
We'll be onto them.

440
00:42:56,970 --> 00:42:58,740
Come on!

441
00:43:01,770 --> 00:43:02,970
Come on!

442
00:43:04,090 --> 00:43:05,870
Give the signal!

443
00:43:06,490 --> 00:43:07,590
Come on!

444
00:43:15,570 --> 00:43:17,370
What will we do, sir?

445
00:43:23,370 --> 00:43:24,870
Great Darius.

446
00:43:25,690 --> 00:43:27,890
I had doubts, now I'm sure.

447
00:43:28,640 --> 00:43:30,590
Tell the archers.
We won't attack.

448
00:43:32,720 --> 00:43:34,740
What do you mean?

449
00:43:34,740 --> 00:43:38,590
İbrahim Fakih and Barkın won't
get revealed, Nikola.

450
00:43:39,820 --> 00:43:41,920
We'll do it another way.

451
00:43:42,070 --> 00:43:43,340
This is an ambush.

452
00:43:44,420 --> 00:43:45,620
What does this mean?

453
00:43:46,020 --> 00:43:48,320
Osman and the others took
my castle.

454
00:43:48,770 --> 00:43:50,320
I'll destroy them.

455
00:43:53,570 --> 00:43:55,920
What do you suggest doing?

456
00:44:07,020 --> 00:44:07,970
My bey.

457
00:44:08,370 --> 00:44:11,020
The Mongols set the ambush.
It's apparent.

458
00:44:11,990 --> 00:44:14,495
It's apparent.
It is.

459
00:44:15,980 --> 00:44:24,760
The ones who attacked Barkın Bey
and killed Umur Bey are the Mongols.

460
00:44:29,740 --> 00:44:32,390
We gave you a hard time, Barkın Bey.

461
00:44:33,670 --> 00:44:36,850
But caution saves lives.

462
00:44:39,250 --> 00:44:40,460
Give us your blessing.

463
00:44:41,090 --> 00:44:42,340
It's yours, Osman Bey.

464
00:44:42,650 --> 00:44:46,700
Now get your alps and head to Aksu.
We'll follow you.

465
00:44:49,040 --> 00:44:50,050
Alright, my bey.

466
00:44:50,770 --> 00:44:52,050
Alps, come on.

467
00:45:11,600 --> 00:45:12,440
Konur.

468
00:45:16,340 --> 00:45:18,530
Keep Barkın Bey followed.

469
00:45:18,890 --> 00:45:21,040
He'll always be followed by
three alps.

470
00:45:21,400 --> 00:45:22,770
As you order, my bey.

471
00:45:24,860 --> 00:45:25,770
Boran.

472
00:45:26,410 --> 00:45:27,220
My bey.

473
00:45:27,700 --> 00:45:32,340
When Turgut Bey and Kosses comes,
we'll attack Nikola's caravan.

474
00:45:32,920 --> 00:45:34,970
As you order, my bey.

475
00:45:36,860 --> 00:45:39,570
The wolf won't return
empty-handed, Nikola.

476
00:45:39,960 --> 00:45:41,820
Osman will hunt something.

477
00:45:42,170 --> 00:45:46,100
Osman is waiting for me to kill him.

478
00:46:09,930 --> 00:46:12,800
If we went there,
we would be the prey.

479
00:46:13,960 --> 00:46:17,170
Sometimes, waiting is the only
way to hit.

480
00:46:22,300 --> 00:46:25,400
These idiots were going to
outplay me.

481
00:46:29,860 --> 00:46:33,260
The wind changed its direction.

482
00:46:34,660 --> 00:46:37,060
Today is the end of them all.

483
00:46:37,480 --> 00:46:39,720
Osman will attack that caravan.

484
00:46:40,810 --> 00:46:42,930
Information is everything, Nikola.

485
00:46:43,480 --> 00:46:47,860
We know him. He doesn't
know us.

486
00:46:54,210 --> 00:46:54,930
Come on.

487
00:47:08,470 --> 00:47:13,820
I didn't do it. Please!
Please, help me!

488
00:47:13,880 --> 00:47:17,030
Stop, my girl. Stop.
I will help you.

489
00:47:17,320 --> 00:47:18,860
Stop. Stop.

490
00:47:19,660 --> 00:47:22,680
Look! This is your antidote.

491
00:47:22,800 --> 00:47:27,290
If you tell me about your
treachery, I will give it to you.

492
00:47:28,690 --> 00:47:31,490
I didn't do it.
Mari died.

493
00:47:32,100 --> 00:47:35,060
I didn't do it.
She was my only friend.

494
00:47:35,690 --> 00:47:37,000
I didn't kill her.

495
00:47:38,640 --> 00:47:41,250
Zehra.
Zehra did it.

496
00:47:41,820 --> 00:47:44,480
Zehra poisoned her.

497
00:47:44,570 --> 00:47:46,290
Please!

498
00:47:50,040 --> 00:47:53,430
I saved your life!
How can you do this to me?

499
00:47:53,740 --> 00:47:55,570
Lying dog!

500
00:48:00,890 --> 00:48:02,930
You old hag!

501
00:48:04,020 --> 00:48:08,790
Even if you kill me, you won't
stop the rise of the darkness!

502
00:48:09,260 --> 00:48:11,130
It will be your end!

503
00:48:11,430 --> 00:48:14,860
You slandered my children!

504
00:48:15,260 --> 00:48:19,830
You killed Mari and her child!

505
00:48:19,980 --> 00:48:21,580
Weasel!

506
00:48:26,450 --> 00:48:30,900
Poor Mari, her love for Turgut
blinded her.

507
00:48:31,760 --> 00:48:34,000
She was about to become a Muslim.

508
00:48:34,100 --> 00:48:37,300
I stopped her from her mistake.

509
00:48:39,280 --> 00:48:41,360
It's good that she died.

510
00:48:41,360 --> 00:48:44,790
What did you want from
a poor innocent baby?

511
00:48:44,790 --> 00:48:47,640
What, huh?

512
00:48:49,120 --> 00:48:51,280
A small Muslim Turk...

513
00:48:52,860 --> 00:48:55,980
it's better to crush the head
of the snake when it's small.

514
00:48:55,980 --> 00:49:00,120
Soon, Osman and you will share
the same fate.

515
00:49:00,520 --> 00:49:03,040
You won't stop the darkness!

516
00:49:03,040 --> 00:49:06,600
Enough! Enough!
Silence!

517
00:49:06,600 --> 00:49:09,250
I will kill you!

518
00:49:09,250 --> 00:49:14,070
You will tell me who is controlling you!

519
00:49:14,370 --> 00:49:20,260
Never! Never!
You can never make me speak!

520
00:50:22,450 --> 00:50:24,810
Aren't we supposed to lower the numbers?

521
00:50:24,960 --> 00:50:28,610
It would be more desirable for
Osman.

522
00:50:28,820 --> 00:50:29,880
No.

523
00:50:30,650 --> 00:50:34,560
Nikola, Osman knows the importance
of this caravan.

524
00:50:34,810 --> 00:50:38,940
If you lower the numbers, he'll know
that it's a trap.

525
00:50:40,050 --> 00:50:42,630
So, he will attack?

526
00:50:43,080 --> 00:50:47,020
They see themselves as wolves and
we as sheep.

527
00:50:47,450 --> 00:50:53,350
But we are lions under that disguise.

528
00:51:02,760 --> 00:51:06,090
Argus should lead the caravan.
You should hide.

529
00:51:06,580 --> 00:51:10,560
When Osman attacks you,
I'll come from the rear.

530
00:51:11,000 --> 00:51:15,520
Poor caravan masters will turn out
to be good swordmasters.

531
00:51:16,840 --> 00:51:21,560
Osman will be stuck in between
and get smashed.

532
00:51:22,940 --> 00:51:24,210
Great Darius.

533
00:51:26,040 --> 00:51:31,740
It must be important news since
you hold it tight like that.

534
00:51:33,560 --> 00:51:35,480
There is time, Nikola.

535
00:51:37,100 --> 00:51:38,020
There is time.

536
00:52:06,740 --> 00:52:09,270
Master Darius.

537
00:52:11,270 --> 00:52:13,200
Master of Darkness.

538
00:52:22,150 --> 00:52:26,870
To conquest a castle, you need
to break many things.

539
00:52:29,010 --> 00:52:31,650
It's not only the walls that
protect the castle.

540
00:52:33,920 --> 00:52:37,160
You should break the courage
of their commander.

541
00:52:38,710 --> 00:52:42,340
The trust of his soldiers for him.

542
00:52:43,820 --> 00:52:47,990
And the faith of his people in victory.

543
00:52:53,510 --> 00:52:58,490
Now, this caravan will be like water for
İnegöl.

544
00:52:59,060 --> 00:53:02,040
But it doesn't need a water.

545
00:53:02,690 --> 00:53:05,180
İnegöl is a tree that needs to dry.

546
00:53:07,560 --> 00:53:10,980
If that hidden face is working
with Nikola...

547
00:53:11,910 --> 00:53:13,340
he might be around.

548
00:53:15,700 --> 00:53:18,800
So, we'll be cautious.

549
00:53:37,910 --> 00:53:41,330
-Barkın Bey.
-Speak, Cerkutay.

550
00:53:44,420 --> 00:53:45,980
Barkın Bey.

551
00:53:47,120 --> 00:53:48,960
Are your swords sharp?

552
00:53:49,340 --> 00:53:52,290
If not, let me sharpen them.

553
00:53:53,050 --> 00:53:57,200
My swords are always sharp.
Don't worry.

554
00:53:57,910 --> 00:54:01,010
Good.

555
00:54:20,180 --> 00:54:25,160
We'll take a position all around the road.
But we won't waste goods

556
00:54:26,820 --> 00:54:31,340
We'll use them during our conquests.

557
00:54:34,500 --> 00:54:38,380
Inshallah, the hidden face
will be there.

558
00:54:39,020 --> 00:54:44,710
Inshallah he'll be there and we'll end
that snake who killed Mari.

559
00:54:48,260 --> 00:54:51,510
Let's not forget Nikola, Turgut.

560
00:54:52,400 --> 00:54:58,620
First, his caravan, then his castle,
then his head.

561
00:55:00,010 --> 00:55:01,840
Aren't we late, Osman Bey?

562
00:55:03,440 --> 00:55:05,700
Konur. Boran.

563
00:55:05,970 --> 00:55:07,490
We'll attack from three sides.

564
00:55:09,780 --> 00:55:13,110
But you'll go rear the caravan.

565
00:55:14,240 --> 00:55:20,650
If they have a plan, you will
ruin it as wolves attacking sheep.

566
00:55:21,050 --> 00:55:22,560
We'll do what's necessary.

567
00:55:25,060 --> 00:55:26,450
May Allah bless our efforts.

568
00:55:26,730 --> 00:55:27,690
Amin.

569
00:55:27,930 --> 00:55:29,830
Alps! Come on.

570
00:56:16,370 --> 00:56:19,480
Come here. Come.

571
00:56:57,580 --> 00:57:00,620
Where are you going
without my approval?

572
00:57:02,360 --> 00:57:03,750
These lands belong to Turks.

573
00:57:08,860 --> 00:57:11,510
Give us the tribute, at least.

574
00:57:15,310 --> 00:57:17,950
You are going to help Nikola, huh?

575
00:57:24,540 --> 00:57:25,830
Osman Bey.

576
00:57:27,040 --> 00:57:29,720
I think you need help.

577
00:57:44,780 --> 00:57:48,040
Come here!

578
00:58:12,720 --> 00:58:16,030
Nikola! Nikola!

579
00:58:19,490 --> 00:58:21,890
It's our turn, Turgut.

580
00:58:23,750 --> 00:58:26,130
Let's take this dog's
tooth out.

581
00:58:26,990 --> 00:58:28,510
Let's do it.

582
00:58:28,860 --> 00:58:30,750
Are you ready, Samuel?

583
00:58:30,750 --> 00:58:33,050
Your sword will spill blood now.

584
00:58:33,950 --> 00:58:36,640
Come on!

585
00:59:00,210 --> 00:59:02,010
You snake!

586
00:59:03,140 --> 00:59:05,730
So, you did all the treachery, huh?

587
00:59:06,070 --> 00:59:06,860
You!

588
00:59:48,190 --> 00:59:51,780
You've chosen the wrong side.

589
01:00:10,760 --> 01:00:13,040
Alps, protect yourselves!

590
01:01:01,600 --> 01:01:02,570
My bey!

591
01:01:34,070 --> 01:01:36,410
You disgraceful weasel!

592
01:01:36,660 --> 01:01:39,110
You are the head of the snake.

593
01:01:40,930 --> 01:01:42,940
It's your end now!

594
01:02:08,730 --> 01:02:09,980
Stay down!

595
01:02:15,620 --> 01:02:17,730
Boran! Saltuk!
Catch him.

596
01:02:22,580 --> 01:02:23,900
We are on it, my bey!

597
01:02:47,440 --> 01:02:49,570
I won't allow this, Osman.

598
01:03:35,150 --> 01:03:35,980
Boran!

599
01:04:12,810 --> 01:04:13,830
Master.

600
01:04:18,540 --> 01:04:19,670
Saltuk!

601
01:04:43,880 --> 01:04:44,780
Boran!

602
01:04:51,830 --> 01:04:59,260
I bear witness that there is no god but
Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad

603
01:04:59,400 --> 01:05:02,020
is the servant and Messenger of Allah.

604
01:05:03,710 --> 01:05:04,750
Saltuk.

605
01:05:16,300 --> 01:05:17,040
Master.

606
01:05:26,510 --> 01:05:27,270
Master.

607
01:05:40,180 --> 01:05:41,440
Osman!

608
01:05:58,380 --> 01:05:59,710
You.

609
01:06:23,710 --> 01:06:26,920
Verily we belong to Allah and verily
to Him do we return.

610
01:06:27,390 --> 01:06:28,920
Amin.

611
01:06:29,700 --> 01:06:30,690
Amin.

612
01:06:43,480 --> 01:06:46,880
Darkness won't leave its servants.

613
01:06:48,810 --> 01:06:51,010
I'll save you, Cornelia.

614
01:07:02,420 --> 01:07:04,380
Salam Alaikum.

615
01:07:04,380 --> 01:07:06,590
Alaikum Salam, İbrahim Fakih.

616
01:07:07,480 --> 01:07:11,520
Humans are strange, aren't they,
Kumral Abdal.

617
01:07:11,780 --> 01:07:14,350
The poor girl you opened
your doors for...

618
01:07:14,350 --> 01:07:16,350
the Christian child...

619
01:07:16,680 --> 01:07:20,350
has risked her life
for her Muslim mother, huh?

620
01:07:20,940 --> 01:07:24,130
It is. It's the heart.

621
01:07:25,040 --> 01:07:28,000
Inshallah Allah will destine her
to be Muslim.

622
01:07:28,000 --> 01:07:31,200
Inshallah. Inshallah.
You've spoken well.

623
01:07:31,750 --> 01:07:34,210
How is her health?

624
01:07:34,210 --> 01:07:37,440
It must be bad. We didn't see
her.

625
01:07:39,170 --> 01:07:42,230
I didn't see the wound. They don't
let me in.

626
01:07:43,360 --> 01:07:44,230
She is fine.

627
01:07:45,040 --> 01:07:46,880
We would hear it otherwise.

628
01:07:48,010 --> 01:07:50,200
Alright. Alright.

629
01:07:50,200 --> 01:07:54,360
May Allah heal her, inshallah.

630
01:07:54,360 --> 01:07:56,680
Inshallah.

631
01:08:03,210 --> 01:08:07,400
They know Cornelia.
I can't leave her to them.

632
01:08:38,810 --> 01:08:42,729
Even if you kill me, my master
will bring your end.

633
01:08:43,538 --> 01:08:46,090
One of us dies and a thousand of
us born.

634
01:08:52,749 --> 01:08:53,890
Did she speak, mother?

635
01:08:54,760 --> 01:08:56,729
She has spoken the things
we already know.

636
01:08:58,408 --> 01:09:03,210
But she didn't say who her
master is.

637
01:09:06,109 --> 01:09:08,460
She won't die before Osman Bey
comes, right?

638
01:09:09,460 --> 01:09:13,078
As she pleases. She doesn't
have much time.

639
01:09:13,078 --> 01:09:15,279
If she speaks...

640
01:09:15,279 --> 01:09:17,819
we might let her live.

641
01:09:18,920 --> 01:09:22,288
I know that you won't let me live,
you old hag!

642
01:09:22,788 --> 01:09:23,689
Enough!

643
01:09:27,279 --> 01:09:28,270
Dishonorable.

644
01:09:30,090 --> 01:09:31,118
Heartless.

645
01:09:32,229 --> 01:09:36,170
How did you kill an innocent baby,
Mari who has seen you as a sister?

646
01:09:40,520 --> 01:09:41,868
It was easy.

647
01:09:42,970 --> 01:09:46,060
I sacrificed Mari for
our holy cause.

648
01:09:48,560 --> 01:09:52,300
You all... You all believed me!

649
01:09:52,640 --> 01:09:54,820
You killed Gündüz and Ayşe.

650
01:09:56,870 --> 01:09:58,050
And Zehra too.

651
01:09:58,820 --> 01:10:02,490
You are stupid!
You are stupid!

652
01:10:02,910 --> 01:10:06,140
Your master is the stupid one.

653
01:10:09,310 --> 01:10:12,750
Both Güdüz Bey and Ayşe Hatun
are safe and sound.

654
01:10:20,130 --> 01:10:21,910
Are you talking about me, Cornelia?

655
01:10:32,250 --> 01:10:35,460
Osman Bey went to settle
some scores.

656
01:10:36,900 --> 01:10:40,090
Our hearts are enlightened with
the light of faith.

657
01:10:40,500 --> 01:10:42,650
We'll destroy your darkness.

658
01:10:52,170 --> 01:10:54,064
You weasel!

659
01:10:54,220 --> 01:10:56,260
You won't die before suffering!

660
01:11:05,080 --> 01:11:06,840
Get ready, Cornelia.

661
01:11:07,520 --> 01:11:09,660
This is the sound of the Gream Reaper.

662
01:12:51,120 --> 01:12:52,860
Did Cornelia speak, mother?

663
01:12:58,140 --> 01:12:59,540
She has.

664
01:13:00,060 --> 01:13:01,460
It's just as we thought.

665
01:13:02,340 --> 01:13:04,560
She was behind everything.

666
01:13:05,040 --> 01:13:08,760
Cornelia is the traitor among us.

667
01:13:11,400 --> 01:13:12,780
What are you saying, mother?

668
01:13:15,140 --> 01:13:16,040
Cornelia?

669
01:13:18,120 --> 01:13:19,820
Did Cornelia do this to Mari?

670
01:13:21,120 --> 01:13:21,820
No.

671
01:13:23,000 --> 01:13:24,460
It's not possible.

672
01:13:24,680 --> 01:13:27,020
Mari and Cornelia were like
sisters!

673
01:13:27,320 --> 01:13:28,640
It must be a mistake.

674
01:13:28,640 --> 01:13:30,300
We'll find out, Kosses.

675
01:13:30,480 --> 01:13:31,920
We'll find it all out.

676
01:13:32,300 --> 01:13:34,560
But let's confirm this weasel first.

677
01:14:05,920 --> 01:14:08,820
Demon! You will suffer!

678
01:14:12,000 --> 01:14:13,620
Even if you kill me...

679
01:14:14,700 --> 01:14:16,480
my master will finish you.

680
01:14:19,160 --> 01:14:20,740
We killed your master.

681
01:14:22,200 --> 01:14:25,980
No. No. You can't do that.

682
01:14:25,980 --> 01:14:27,980
You aren't strong enough
to kill him.

683
01:14:28,140 --> 01:14:28,920
We are.

684
01:14:32,260 --> 01:14:34,320
It was easy.

685
01:14:36,880 --> 01:14:40,940
Now, let's take you to your master.

686
01:14:47,480 --> 01:14:49,600
Get up!

687
01:14:53,220 --> 01:14:54,400
Your mouth.

688
01:14:59,980 --> 01:15:01,060
Move!

689
01:15:39,240 --> 01:15:43,140
No. You couldn't do that.

690
01:15:45,220 --> 01:15:46,700
How did you kill him?

691
01:15:50,220 --> 01:15:51,680
My master!

692
01:15:55,000 --> 01:15:56,400
Stop crying!

693
01:15:59,760 --> 01:16:01,900
You will speak in front of
everyone.

694
01:16:05,380 --> 01:16:07,460
Did you kill Mari?

695
01:16:17,640 --> 01:16:20,260
Why aren't you answering?
Did you kill my Mari?

696
01:16:20,260 --> 01:16:21,860
Why don't you answer?

697
01:16:21,860 --> 01:16:24,400
Speak, woman?
Did you kill her?

698
01:16:24,400 --> 01:16:25,460
Speak!

699
01:16:29,620 --> 01:16:35,080
I sacrificed Mari to the darkness
for our holy cause.

700
01:16:36,370 --> 01:16:40,160
You traitor! She saw you
as a sister!

701
01:16:40,160 --> 01:16:41,700
I will kill you!

702
01:16:41,700 --> 01:16:42,580
Kosses!

703
01:16:44,080 --> 01:16:45,020
Turgut Bey!

704
01:16:54,320 --> 01:16:56,280
She isn't alone, Osman Bey.

705
01:16:56,440 --> 01:16:58,580
Who is behind you?

706
01:16:58,580 --> 01:17:00,160
Who made you do this?

707
01:17:00,160 --> 01:17:01,220
Turgut Bey.

708
01:17:26,580 --> 01:17:28,440
Was it him?

709
01:17:41,280 --> 01:17:42,380
Speak!

710
01:17:50,180 --> 01:17:51,100
Master.

711
01:17:54,020 --> 01:17:54,900
Master.

712
01:17:55,160 --> 01:17:56,320
My master.

713
01:17:58,220 --> 01:18:01,020
You killed him.

714
01:18:03,640 --> 01:18:04,960
Speak.

715
01:18:05,640 --> 01:18:08,270
Did you do the Söğüt explosion?

716
01:18:09,640 --> 01:18:14,840
My master died but the others
are still alive.

717
01:18:15,920 --> 01:18:17,620
Your end...

718
01:18:21,490 --> 01:18:24,290
will come from the darkness.

719
01:18:55,190 --> 01:18:56,870
Take them.

720
01:19:20,520 --> 01:19:21,990
O' people!

721
01:19:24,320 --> 01:19:26,270
You all have seen it!

722
01:19:26,770 --> 01:19:28,270
And heard it!

723
01:19:30,370 --> 01:19:38,420
Turgut Bey's wife, Michael Kosses' sister
Mari, and her baby...

724
01:19:40,570 --> 01:19:42,820
was her helper Cornelia.

725
01:19:49,720 --> 01:19:54,870
My brother Gündüz Bey and Ayşe Hatun
were slandered.

726
01:19:59,090 --> 01:20:01,170
They are innocent.

727
01:20:08,120 --> 01:20:13,320
Cornelia and the spawn of darkness
that work with her...

728
01:20:14,540 --> 01:20:18,540
tried to make us fight
each other...

729
01:20:20,320 --> 01:20:22,590
and killed Mari in order to
do that.

730
01:20:26,870 --> 01:20:28,090
Boran.

731
01:20:29,190 --> 01:20:30,420
Come on.

732
01:20:48,940 --> 01:20:50,990
Gündüz Bey!

733
01:20:57,290 --> 01:20:58,370
Brother.

734
01:21:12,620 --> 01:21:15,190
He is alive!

735
01:21:49,490 --> 01:21:50,670
Osman Bey.

736
01:22:04,690 --> 01:22:05,890
Gündüz Bey.

737
01:22:07,790 --> 01:22:09,140
Ayşe Hatun.

738
01:22:10,340 --> 01:22:11,970
Give me your blessing.

739
01:22:13,820 --> 01:22:14,990
I was wrong.

740
01:22:16,020 --> 01:22:17,620
I was wrong. Forgive me.

741
01:22:25,020 --> 01:22:26,070
Forgive me.

742
01:22:29,820 --> 01:22:31,070
It's yours, Turgut Bey.

743
01:22:32,340 --> 01:22:33,490
It's yours.

744
01:22:36,720 --> 01:22:37,790
And you...

745
01:22:39,990 --> 01:22:43,090
trusted me without evidence.

746
01:22:44,870 --> 01:22:46,190
Thank you.

747
01:22:47,120 --> 01:22:48,690
My brother.

748
01:22:49,520 --> 01:22:50,940
Forgive me.

749
01:23:04,220 --> 01:23:06,070
You have our blessings, Turgut Bey.

750
01:23:07,140 --> 01:23:08,140
Thank you.

751
01:23:28,720 --> 01:23:30,840
Thank you too, Kosses.

752
01:23:31,040 --> 01:23:32,440
Thank you.

753
01:23:40,990 --> 01:23:42,540
Son.

754
01:23:48,240 --> 01:23:49,320
Welcome.

755
01:23:49,370 --> 01:23:50,690
Thank you, mother.

756
01:23:55,940 --> 01:23:57,090
Mother.

757
01:23:58,340 --> 01:23:59,220
Mother.

758
01:24:03,040 --> 01:24:04,240
Brother.

759
01:24:17,570 --> 01:24:19,870
Those who killed İhvaz Bey and Umur Bey...

760
01:24:22,020 --> 01:24:25,540
are the ones who attacked Söğüt.

761
01:24:27,570 --> 01:24:28,770
Their intention...

762
01:24:29,690 --> 01:24:31,690
is to make us fight each other.

763
01:24:33,270 --> 01:24:35,320
But we didn't.

764
01:24:36,990 --> 01:24:38,940
They wanted to stop the
conquests...

765
01:24:40,340 --> 01:24:41,720
but we didn't stop.

766
01:24:44,340 --> 01:24:46,040
İnhisar Castle...

767
01:24:47,890 --> 01:24:49,520
belongs to Kayı now!

768
01:24:49,970 --> 01:24:55,420
Long live Osman Bey!

769
01:24:56,520 --> 01:25:04,390
Long live Osman Bey!

770
01:25:06,690 --> 01:25:10,240
Long live Osman Bey!

771
01:25:11,830 --> 01:25:27,670
Long live Osman Bey!

772
01:25:28,240 --> 01:25:33,470
We defeated the ones who wanted
to pull us into darkness.

773
01:25:34,890 --> 01:25:36,340
Thank Allah.

774
01:25:36,470 --> 01:25:41,520
The cause of Allah will spread
to the whole world...

775
01:25:42,870 --> 01:25:44,770
if we step back...

776
01:25:48,640 --> 01:25:51,470
may our swords be red with
our blood!

777
01:25:51,670 --> 01:26:28,500
Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

778
01:26:28,550 --> 01:26:31,500
İnegöl Castle

779
01:26:51,890 --> 01:26:57,240
Matheus. It's like you just
saw a ghost.

780
01:27:06,890 --> 01:27:09,220
Do you know what this is?

781
01:27:11,470 --> 01:27:13,590
It's a mark of war.

782
01:27:14,320 --> 01:27:17,840
Only the brave men have it.

783
01:27:18,420 --> 01:27:24,840
Not the idiots who flee from
their castles.

784
01:27:27,790 --> 01:27:29,670
Won't you sit?

785
01:27:39,820 --> 01:27:45,090
Matheus. Forgive my
curiosity.

786
01:27:49,140 --> 01:27:51,620
How did you flee your castle?

787
01:27:53,290 --> 01:27:54,640
A soldier.

788
01:27:56,490 --> 01:27:59,020
A loyal soldier helped me escape.

789
01:28:00,490 --> 01:28:03,170
A loyal soldier.

790
01:28:07,940 --> 01:28:09,820
Loyal, huh?

791
01:28:10,120 --> 01:28:14,240
Loyal? The loyal ones have died, Matheus!

792
01:28:14,240 --> 01:28:18,720
The rest are the ones who surrendered.
Just like you!

793
01:28:19,870 --> 01:28:23,940
Osman released you on purpose.

794
01:28:23,940 --> 01:28:27,690
I lost many things today!

795
01:28:27,690 --> 01:28:33,440
I lost my master who taught
me everything!

796
01:28:33,440 --> 01:28:39,290
And you will lose something too!

797
01:28:39,940 --> 01:28:42,140
You will too!

798
01:28:58,590 --> 01:29:00,420
Master Darius?

799
01:29:01,340 --> 01:29:03,590
You didn't lose me, Nikola.

800
01:29:04,590 --> 01:29:06,640
But our cause is wounded.

801
01:29:07,070 --> 01:29:09,390
Osman ruined our plans...

802
01:29:09,670 --> 01:29:15,190
and took my most capable
student.

803
01:29:34,990 --> 01:29:40,090
Thank Allah. We avenged my father
and uncle, Selvi.

804
01:29:40,420 --> 01:29:43,890
We can sleep in peace now.

805
01:29:44,270 --> 01:29:47,940
Thank Osman Bey, sister.

806
01:29:54,640 --> 01:29:58,540
It's Nawruz time. Spring is here.

807
01:29:59,240 --> 01:30:01,890
It's my first spring with Kayı.

808
01:30:02,120 --> 01:30:03,490
Mashallah.

809
01:30:04,890 --> 01:30:08,640
Orhan. My lion, are you a big brother?

810
01:30:08,840 --> 01:30:10,640
He is a big brother!

811
01:30:11,540 --> 01:30:15,240
Mashallah, ladies!
Evangel!

812
01:30:18,840 --> 01:30:22,390
His teeth are like latches,
his way is Allah's way!

813
01:30:22,720 --> 01:30:26,020
The evil people should stay
away from him!

814
01:30:26,170 --> 01:30:28,490
The dreams of the tyrants
will be ruined.

815
01:30:28,490 --> 01:30:32,390
My great Orhan!
My great Orhan!

816
01:30:32,640 --> 01:30:36,820
He shall ride his horse,
his way shall be light.

817
01:30:36,820 --> 01:30:39,240
He shall enter the water
but won't get wet.

818
01:30:39,240 --> 01:30:42,240
His sharp weapon shall never
get rusted.

819
01:30:42,240 --> 01:30:46,620
Oh, my great Orhan!

820
01:30:46,840 --> 01:30:48,290
Mashallah, mother.

821
01:30:48,690 --> 01:30:53,620
His teeth were visible. He must've
waited for you to grow them, mother.

822
01:30:55,320 --> 01:30:57,140
Mashallah to my Orhan.

823
01:30:57,970 --> 01:31:02,040
So, mother. We need to
dress Orhan now.

824
01:31:02,940 --> 01:31:07,490
Wouldn't I, my girl?
He deserves all the clothes!

825
01:31:14,440 --> 01:31:16,020
Come here.

826
01:31:21,170 --> 01:31:24,320
Mother, why did you rip it off?

827
01:31:25,640 --> 01:31:27,520
It's the customs, Aygül.

828
01:31:28,040 --> 01:31:31,340
It's for his teeth to grow easily.

829
01:31:32,170 --> 01:31:36,970
Yes, ladies. We should help him.

830
01:31:43,090 --> 01:31:46,320
We've overcome all the traps
they set before us.

831
01:31:47,040 --> 01:31:49,540
We defeated the dogs
of the devil.

832
01:31:49,890 --> 01:31:54,290
It's all because of your
trust for me.

833
01:31:55,640 --> 01:31:57,120
Thank you.

834
01:31:58,070 --> 01:31:59,340
Thank you, my bey.

835
01:32:00,220 --> 01:32:05,640
Now, our way and friends
are apparent.

836
01:32:07,190 --> 01:32:08,440
Geyve.

837
01:32:09,770 --> 01:32:13,120
Nekece. Aksu.

838
01:32:14,470 --> 01:32:15,840
Lefke.

839
01:32:19,170 --> 01:32:20,890
And Gemlik.

840
01:32:24,840 --> 01:32:26,020
Inshallah...

841
01:32:26,990 --> 01:32:31,270
we'll raise the flag of Kayı there.

842
01:32:36,520 --> 01:32:38,770
As we talked about before, we sent
the scouts.

843
01:32:38,890 --> 01:32:42,220
We won't let a single caravan go to
İnegöl now.

844
01:32:43,890 --> 01:32:46,740
And I informed all the lords.

845
01:32:47,220 --> 01:32:49,790
Whoever trades with İnegöl...

846
01:32:49,790 --> 01:32:53,890
will face our sanctions.

847
01:32:54,290 --> 01:32:57,220
We surrounded them, Osman Bey.

848
01:32:59,020 --> 01:33:03,340
We'll go to the oppressed
with the sword of justice.

849
01:33:04,170 --> 01:33:06,020
We'll stop their suffering.

850
01:33:06,570 --> 01:33:09,270
We'll kill the tyrants.

851
01:33:13,290 --> 01:33:14,890
But firstly...

852
01:33:15,590 --> 01:33:20,070
the head of the tyrants,
Nikola.

853
01:33:24,220 --> 01:33:26,320
You aren't dead.

854
01:33:31,220 --> 01:33:32,670
The mask?

855
01:33:37,770 --> 01:33:39,620
It was someone else!

856
01:33:46,220 --> 01:33:47,740
It was a game?

857
01:33:49,220 --> 01:33:51,370
And you didn't tell me.

858
01:33:51,870 --> 01:33:53,370
I didn't.

859
01:33:54,240 --> 01:33:57,020
I couldn't, Nikola.

860
01:33:57,390 --> 01:33:59,020
For our cause.

861
01:34:00,620 --> 01:34:04,690
I'm so sorry for what you lost,
Master Darius.

862
01:34:06,270 --> 01:34:11,220
Osman took something from all of us.

863
01:34:17,340 --> 01:34:20,770
Yes, Osman wounded us severely.

864
01:34:21,070 --> 01:34:23,990
But we also took something
important from him.

865
01:34:24,520 --> 01:34:25,990
His suspicion.

866
01:34:26,340 --> 01:34:28,790
He thinks that he destroyed us.

867
01:34:29,370 --> 01:34:32,440
I won't stop, master.

868
01:34:33,320 --> 01:34:35,040
I'll destroy him.

869
01:34:36,120 --> 01:34:38,390
I'll destroy all his dreams...

870
01:34:39,120 --> 01:34:42,240
his goals.

871
01:34:42,670 --> 01:34:44,620
I will destroy him.

872
01:34:47,740 --> 01:34:51,590
-When the time comes, Nikola.
-The time!

873
01:34:52,390 --> 01:34:55,820
I choose the time now, master!

874
01:34:57,140 --> 01:34:58,390
I...

875
01:34:59,220 --> 01:35:00,970
won't wait!

876
01:35:03,840 --> 01:35:05,440
I won't stop!

877
01:35:06,690 --> 01:35:08,440
Whatever is in my castle!

878
01:35:08,990 --> 01:35:12,190
Diamond, ruby, gold, precious metals!

879
01:35:12,190 --> 01:35:15,390
I will sell whatever I have!
All of it!

880
01:35:15,390 --> 01:35:18,490
I will gather everyone from everywhere!

881
01:35:18,490 --> 01:35:22,090
I will get everyone here!
Whoever sells his sword!

882
01:35:22,290 --> 01:35:23,670
All of them!

883
01:35:23,970 --> 01:35:26,420
I have only one goal now!

884
01:35:28,140 --> 01:35:32,370
It is not reviving!

885
01:35:33,490 --> 01:35:36,920
I will bury the Turks where Rome lays!

886
01:35:37,690 --> 01:35:38,920
Nikola!

887
01:35:40,190 --> 01:35:42,490
The war here is stopping.

888
01:35:43,590 --> 01:35:49,890
Emperor Andronikos and Sultan Mesud will
sign a peace treaty.

889
01:35:49,890 --> 01:35:52,970
No! No! No!

890
01:35:53,140 --> 01:35:58,720
Master Arius, do you think I, Nikola...

891
01:35:58,720 --> 01:36:04,020
...would listen to that stupid emperor or
poor Sultan?

892
01:36:04,990 --> 01:36:08,920
Osman will die!

893
01:36:12,020 --> 01:36:15,840
He will die in my hands!

894
01:36:26,540 --> 01:36:31,690
From now on, we will sharpen our swords
for Inegöl Castle.

895
01:36:31,990 --> 01:36:37,390
All of them will be sharpened to kill the
infidels in İnegöl Castle.

896
01:36:39,820 --> 01:36:42,590
I, son of Ertugrul Gazi, Osman Bey...

897
01:36:43,370 --> 01:36:48,490
...swords will not be lowered until
Inegol is conquered, I order!

898
01:36:57,320 --> 01:37:00,570
Inegöl's walls will not be able to stop
us!

899
01:37:03,790 --> 01:37:06,670
-Can I come in, my Bey?
-Come in!

900
01:37:13,340 --> 01:37:15,770
There is news from Sultan Mesud, my Bey.

901
01:37:47,840 --> 01:37:49,620
Sultan Mesud...

902
01:37:52,090 --> 01:37:54,220
...is waiting for me in the tavern.

903
01:38:14,720 --> 01:38:18,390
Saltuk too drank the martyrdom sherbet,
brothers.

904
01:38:23,470 --> 01:38:25,540
We lost many brothers, Boran.

905
01:38:27,070 --> 01:38:28,720
We lost many brothers.

906
01:38:30,870 --> 01:38:32,420
We didn't lose them.

907
01:38:33,990 --> 01:38:35,420
We bid farewell to them.

908
01:38:35,790 --> 01:38:38,720
Right, we bid farewell to them.

909
01:38:41,240 --> 01:38:42,790
To that holy place.

910
01:38:43,990 --> 01:38:45,140
To heaven.

911
01:38:46,470 --> 01:38:48,370
I hope, brother.

912
01:38:52,020 --> 01:38:56,240
Thankfully, Saltuk's revenge was taken.

913
01:38:57,380 --> 01:38:59,600
But still my heart aches, brothers.

914
01:39:02,470 --> 01:39:03,990
No one can fill his place...

915
01:39:06,310 --> 01:39:07,420
...their places.

916
01:39:13,380 --> 01:39:15,280
Cerkutay, I am hungry!

917
01:39:15,360 --> 01:39:17,440
Who is here!

918
01:39:17,500 --> 01:39:19,820
My valiant Kayı is here!
Are you hungry?

919
01:39:20,200 --> 01:39:22,620
Whenever I am hungry...

920
01:39:22,870 --> 01:39:24,960
...I find myself here as well.

921
01:39:28,700 --> 01:39:31,700
Cerkutay always finds something to eat.

922
01:39:35,580 --> 01:39:39,100
Let's eat! Come on.
Come on.

923
01:39:39,310 --> 01:39:40,800
-Ayran.
-Yes it is.

924
01:39:41,000 --> 01:39:43,390
First, say ''Bismillah''.

925
01:39:43,390 --> 01:39:47,680
-Bismillah.
-Well done! Open your mouth.

926
01:39:47,680 --> 01:39:53,960
Horses are coming, they are coming,
coming! Hop! Well done, my valiant!

927
01:39:57,040 --> 01:39:58,870
Eat fast, go fast.

928
01:40:01,280 --> 01:40:02,260
Cerkutay...

929
01:40:03,470 --> 01:40:05,420
...we lost Saltuk but...

930
01:40:05,890 --> 01:40:08,980
...Kayı is our comrade now.

931
01:40:10,540 --> 01:40:11,570
He is.

932
01:40:12,260 --> 01:40:15,970
He is! My valiant Kayı!

933
01:40:27,700 --> 01:40:29,130
Praise be!

934
01:40:30,860 --> 01:40:33,790
-Father.
-What did you say?

935
01:40:34,630 --> 01:40:35,750
Father.

936
01:40:37,350 --> 01:40:38,460
Did you say ''father''?

937
01:40:39,780 --> 01:40:40,860
He said ''father''!

938
01:40:48,180 --> 01:40:49,100
He said ''father''!

939
01:40:49,250 --> 01:40:50,920
-Father.
-Father!

940
01:40:54,460 --> 01:40:57,240
-Father.
-As long as you call me father...

941
01:41:02,900 --> 01:41:04,500
...I will call you...

942
01:41:07,590 --> 01:41:08,960
...Kayı Saltuk.

943
01:41:13,840 --> 01:41:15,400
Kayı Saltuk Alp.

944
01:41:17,100 --> 01:41:19,000
May you be brave as my brother
Saltuk...

945
01:41:20,350 --> 01:41:22,950
...and trustworthy as my brother
Saltuk.

946
01:41:26,370 --> 01:41:28,310
Söğüt

947
01:41:31,260 --> 01:41:32,760
Oh, people!

948
01:41:33,610 --> 01:41:36,130
It is a happy day for the people of Söğüt!

949
01:41:37,080 --> 01:41:38,890
The protector of the Anatolian land...

950
01:41:39,380 --> 01:41:41,100
...the sharp sword of Islam

951
01:41:41,400 --> 01:41:47,320
...the greatest Sultan ever,
Mighty Sultan Mesud is coming to Söğüt!

952
01:41:51,230 --> 01:41:55,560
We will destroy all that is ingrained
in them!

953
01:41:56,270 --> 01:41:57,100
Wake up!

954
01:42:02,460 --> 01:42:04,980
You are the first ones awake!

955
01:42:05,300 --> 01:42:07,170
You woke up to destroy!

956
01:42:10,090 --> 01:42:11,880
Not only Sultan Mesud!

957
01:42:12,600 --> 01:42:14,530
The great commander of the Greek
lands...

958
01:42:14,700 --> 01:42:17,600
...Emperor Andronikos is also coming to
Söğüt!

959
01:42:24,790 --> 01:42:26,150
I don't understand.

960
01:42:26,150 --> 01:42:27,880
-What?
-Why?

961
01:42:29,780 --> 01:42:34,250
The negotiation in the tavern will
conclude Osman Bey's decision.

962
01:42:52,230 --> 01:42:54,670
His Highness, Sultan Mesud.

963
01:43:03,870 --> 01:43:06,580
He is coming!
He is coming!

964
01:43:07,550 --> 01:43:09,150
Welcome, my Sultan!

965
01:43:09,280 --> 01:43:11,200
-Welcome, my Sultan!
-Welcome, my Sultan!

966
01:43:11,450 --> 01:43:17,930
Welcome, my Sultan! We are so glad to
see you, my Sultan.

967
01:43:24,630 --> 01:43:29,930
Welcome, my Sultan!
Welcome, my Sultan!

968
01:43:30,180 --> 01:43:32,510
Welcome, my Sultan!

969
01:43:32,610 --> 01:43:33,500
Hold everywhere.

970
01:43:33,790 --> 01:43:36,780
Close the entrances and exits until
the Sultan leaves.

971
01:44:04,040 --> 01:44:06,230
Aghas, no one can enter.

972
01:44:06,230 --> 01:44:09,410
We are the people of Söğüt.
Also, Osman Bey knows us.

973
01:44:09,410 --> 01:44:11,410
-Let us in.
-Don't wait here.

974
01:44:28,580 --> 01:44:32,450
-Who is that?
-I hope this is good news.

975
01:44:33,280 --> 01:44:37,730
The Emperor.

976
01:44:44,360 --> 01:44:46,580
I hope this is good news.

977
01:45:31,420 --> 01:45:34,230
What kind of pain is this, mother?

978
01:45:34,620 --> 01:45:36,140
It comes and goes.

979
01:45:36,420 --> 01:45:38,140
Toothache is hard, my girl.

980
01:45:38,420 --> 01:45:40,560
I will prepare some medicine for you.

981
01:45:40,560 --> 01:45:42,100
You have to wait a while.

982
01:45:42,100 --> 01:45:44,210
Bt you will get better, I hope.

983
01:45:47,240 --> 01:45:49,500
The Emperor is in Söğüt, mother.

984
01:45:51,570 --> 01:45:53,220
This makes me worry.

985
01:45:53,360 --> 01:45:55,010
I hope it is good news.

986
01:45:55,870 --> 01:46:01,590
Since both Emperor and Sultan Mesud came
to my Osman's feet...

987
01:46:01,800 --> 01:46:03,590
...I am sure it is good news.

988
01:46:04,150 --> 01:46:05,590
I hope, mother.

989
01:46:05,710 --> 01:46:10,140
They played many games but we destroyed
them all with Allah's help, thankfully.

990
01:46:15,030 --> 01:46:16,800
Thankfully, we did.

991
01:46:17,100 --> 01:46:21,200
We did it with the strength Allah gave us.

992
01:46:21,330 --> 01:46:22,460
May it always be.

993
01:46:23,480 --> 01:46:25,330
Come on, drink this.

994
01:46:26,130 --> 01:46:27,870
May it be healing.

995
01:46:29,450 --> 01:46:31,390
In the name of Allah.

996
01:46:40,100 --> 01:46:41,630
Welcome, Osman Bey!

997
01:46:41,630 --> 01:46:44,800
Welcome, Osman Bey!
Welcome, Osman Bey!

998
01:46:45,220 --> 01:46:47,270
Welcome, Osman Bey!

999
01:46:47,380 --> 01:46:51,840
-Welcome, Osman Bey!
-Welcome, Osman Bey!

1000
01:46:52,020 --> 01:46:55,580
Stay cautious. We may be surprised.

1001
01:46:55,610 --> 01:46:57,500
Welcome, Osman Bey!

1002
01:46:57,500 --> 01:47:00,060
Welcome, Osman Bey!
Welcome, Osman Bey!

1003
01:47:03,240 --> 01:47:04,630
Your sword, Osman Bey.

1004
01:47:44,580 --> 01:47:46,330
I know about what happened, Nikola.

1005
01:47:47,310 --> 01:47:53,750
But know that no anger, no revenge will
prevent this peace.

1006
01:47:55,810 --> 01:47:58,390
Of course, my Beloved Emperor.

1007
01:47:59,570 --> 01:48:02,010
I lost all my power but...

1008
01:48:02,120 --> 01:48:07,730
...Rome! May Rome always live!

1009
01:48:08,480 --> 01:48:12,700
Nikola, your personal anger is gone
the minute you sit at this table.

1010
01:48:14,050 --> 01:48:18,600
We will expand the union agreement
we signed with Geyhatu...

1011
01:48:19,320 --> 01:48:21,890
...and sign it with Sultan Mesud as well.

1012
01:48:26,610 --> 01:48:27,590
Aya Nikola...

1013
01:48:28,920 --> 01:48:31,060
...I once accepted your testimony.

1014
01:48:31,580 --> 01:48:34,200
Once, sent an army upon you.

1015
01:48:35,040 --> 01:48:37,620
But today is about peace.

1016
01:48:38,440 --> 01:48:42,900
Neither you nor Osman can't prevent this.

1017
01:48:44,750 --> 01:48:47,000
Honorable Sultan...

1018
01:48:48,040 --> 01:48:51,450
...everything you say will happen, today.

1019
01:49:00,030 --> 01:49:01,330
But tomorrow...

1020
01:49:11,570 --> 01:49:13,410
Your Highness, Sultan Mesud.

1021
01:49:18,060 --> 01:49:19,850
Emperor Andronikos.

1022
01:49:22,640 --> 01:49:28,320
...everywhere will be covered in blood.

1023
01:49:29,850 --> 01:49:31,300
Nikola!

1024
01:49:34,570 --> 01:49:36,250
Osman Bey!

1025
01:50:03,370 --> 01:50:05,050
We must inform Master Arius.

1026
01:50:05,760 --> 01:50:08,780
Go find him and inform him.

1027
01:50:09,350 --> 01:50:12,850
Tell him we are ready to kill everyone in
the tavern if the Master orders.

1028
01:50:19,980 --> 01:50:20,900
Osman Bey...

1029
01:50:22,700 --> 01:50:29,920
...the treaty you signed with the Lords
and Emperor Andronikos will be extended.

1030
01:50:32,410 --> 01:50:37,280
The State of Seljuk will be a part of this
treaty.

1031
01:50:37,490 --> 01:50:42,050
Of course, with new conditions and
additions.

1032
01:50:47,230 --> 01:50:53,380
Geyhatu is prisoned by Argun Khan.

1033
01:50:54,680 --> 01:50:56,760
Nökers are not under one roof.

1034
01:50:57,520 --> 01:50:58,990
They come in parts.

1035
01:50:59,640 --> 01:51:03,890
Thus, they are not dangerous.

1036
01:51:04,470 --> 01:51:09,830
I won't back off from my fight and my
conquest.

1037
01:51:12,890 --> 01:51:16,230
Osman Bey, you took İnhisar.

1038
01:51:16,930 --> 01:51:19,880
You killed the Lord of Inhisar, Mateus.

1039
01:51:20,120 --> 01:51:25,130
All these are enough reasons for me to
send you an army.

1040
01:51:44,610 --> 01:51:46,030
Andronikos is right.

1041
01:51:48,090 --> 01:51:52,620
You took advantage of Geyhatu's absence
and attacked immediately, Osman Bey.

1042
01:51:52,740 --> 01:51:57,700
A Bey's responsibility is to protect
his lands first...

1043
01:51:58,790 --> 01:52:01,010
...then attack.

1044
01:52:05,590 --> 01:52:07,640
We had a common enemy so we
made a deal.

1045
01:52:08,580 --> 01:52:11,560
But there is no deal from now on.

1046
01:52:12,460 --> 01:52:18,210
Two countries are here looking for a way
for peace, Osman Bey!

1047
01:52:18,930 --> 01:52:20,820
You can't act on your own.

1048
01:52:20,820 --> 01:52:23,600
We want this for the safety f the people.

1049
01:52:24,110 --> 01:52:28,460
Am I defeated so that I have to make a
deal I don't want to!

1050
01:52:28,460 --> 01:52:31,660
We are forgiving what you had done,
Osman Bey.

1051
01:52:32,060 --> 01:52:34,540
I've done nothing to be forgiven.

1052
01:52:40,080 --> 01:52:41,490
To no one.

1053
01:52:44,890 --> 01:52:45,880
But...

1054
01:52:46,730 --> 01:52:48,880
...since you want peace...

1055
01:52:50,090 --> 01:52:55,620
...in that case, I want Aksu's and
Karaçapuş's taxes.

1056
01:53:01,580 --> 01:53:06,400
And I would like to graze my animals
in the pastures around it.

1057
01:53:11,750 --> 01:53:15,390
I want the Turkmens who want to come
to far away tribes and see prosperity...

1058
01:53:15,390 --> 01:53:17,460
...to be led the way.

1059
01:53:20,740 --> 01:53:25,930
I want everyone who says they are
going to Osman Bey to be allowed.

1060
01:53:26,730 --> 01:53:31,560
I want them to be given horses, swords.

1061
01:53:34,000 --> 01:53:35,300
For Nikola...

1062
01:53:36,950 --> 01:53:42,180
...I have the mines he has from now on.

1063
01:53:50,070 --> 01:53:51,480
I said my conditions.

1064
01:53:53,450 --> 01:53:55,090
You've heard.

1065
01:53:56,440 --> 01:53:59,040
If there are two countries at this table
...

1066
01:54:01,520 --> 01:54:03,750
...then we must negotiate.

1067
01:54:08,470 --> 01:54:11,530
Tell me, I am listening.

1068
01:54:30,740 --> 01:54:34,190
It is really hard to convince the Lords
of these conditions.

1069
01:54:43,790 --> 01:54:45,160
But I accept.

1070
01:55:05,020 --> 01:55:05,940
Clerk.

1071
01:55:10,640 --> 01:55:12,490
Nikola!

1072
01:55:30,340 --> 01:55:31,510
Osman Bey.

1073
01:55:41,790 --> 01:55:46,120
You got what you wanted again, right?

1074
01:55:51,850 --> 01:55:55,240
But your soul is still inside your body,
Nikola.

1075
01:55:57,940 --> 01:56:03,750
I don't give a damn about the treaty these
two old men made.

1076
01:56:06,110 --> 01:56:10,000
Do you know that I will kill you, right?
With my own hands.

1077
01:56:14,460 --> 01:56:17,040
If you dare to break this treaty...

1078
01:56:18,930 --> 01:56:20,220
...I will be waiting.

1079
01:56:23,840 --> 01:56:29,250
Then, I will kill you with my sword.

1080
01:56:37,810 --> 01:56:40,070
You see how calm I am, don't you?

1081
01:56:42,930 --> 01:56:45,390
This is the calm before the storm.

1082
01:57:00,860 --> 01:57:02,240
Nikola!

1083
01:57:12,080 --> 01:57:13,700
We had to do this.

1084
01:57:14,950 --> 01:57:20,400
A leader can have no other purpose than
to keep the state standing.

1085
01:57:33,770 --> 01:57:38,250
Don't worry Sultan Mesud.
We didn't make a mistake.

1086
01:57:39,520 --> 01:57:44,820
This peace will reign in this land
for decades.

1087
01:57:45,960 --> 01:57:49,850
That's enough time to breathe
a sigh of relief.

1088
01:57:50,420 --> 01:57:53,430
Making peace is easy, Emperor.

1089
01:57:54,100 --> 01:57:57,190
The hard thing is to make it permanent.

1090
01:57:57,780 --> 01:58:02,140
I am sure you will do your part
in this matter.

1091
01:58:03,600 --> 01:58:06,550
I want to trust you as well, Sultan Mesud.

1092
01:58:15,740 --> 01:58:18,880
To a lasting peace, Emperor.

1093
01:58:30,740 --> 01:58:32,350
My Orhan!

1094
01:58:32,900 --> 01:58:34,380
Malhun...

1095
01:58:34,380 --> 01:58:37,490
...did you distribute my Orhan's boiled
wheat to the whole tribe?

1096
01:58:37,540 --> 01:58:40,540
The Hatuns did it, mother.

1097
01:58:45,300 --> 01:58:48,490
Zehra, bring the tray. Come on.

1098
01:59:17,700 --> 01:59:19,950
What did you choose, my lion son?

1099
01:59:24,980 --> 01:59:28,400
Your mother couldn't see what you
chose.

1100
01:59:29,410 --> 01:59:32,430
Your mother doesn't know.
She didn't see, this poor woman.

1101
01:59:35,110 --> 01:59:36,450
Hatuns!

1102
01:59:38,290 --> 01:59:41,760
My Kayı chose an Akça(money).

1103
01:59:43,270 --> 01:59:48,110
-Did you?
-My valiant will be an honest merchant!

1104
01:59:49,400 --> 01:59:52,900
Will you be a merchant, my lion son?

1105
02:00:01,180 --> 02:00:03,580
Stand up. Come on, my girl.

1106
02:00:03,720 --> 02:00:06,240
In the name of Allah!

1107
02:00:06,450 --> 02:00:11,030
May you be a good son to your mother
and your father!

1108
02:00:11,460 --> 02:00:13,350
-Amen!
-Amen!

1109
02:00:13,490 --> 02:00:16,870
Let your pockets overflow like these
wheat.

1110
02:00:17,040 --> 02:00:17,890
Amen!

1111
02:00:18,040 --> 02:00:22,010
May your heart and life be blessed
like this!

1112
02:00:23,030 --> 02:00:25,860
May your worst be strong.

1113
02:00:27,140 --> 02:00:30,120
May Allah increase your knowledge!

1114
02:00:31,660 --> 02:00:35,700
May your sword always be sharp
against the oppressors.

1115
02:00:35,840 --> 02:00:37,980
-Amen!
-Amen!

1116
02:00:38,940 --> 02:00:40,840
In the name of Allah!

1117
02:00:42,120 --> 02:00:44,520
In the name of Allah!
My Valiant!

1118
02:00:45,780 --> 02:00:48,520
Let's see which one my valiant chooses.

1119
02:00:48,760 --> 02:00:51,440
Come on, our valiant!
What will you choose?

1120
02:00:54,460 --> 02:00:57,290
Praise be!
Praise be!

1121
02:00:59,200 --> 02:01:02,770
-Praise be to my lion!
-Praise be!

1122
02:01:02,840 --> 02:01:04,640
Praise be! Mother...

1123
02:01:05,260 --> 02:01:07,540
...Aktemur chose an inkstand, remember?

1124
02:01:07,670 --> 02:01:08,540
Right!

1125
02:01:15,160 --> 02:01:17,670
Let's see what Alaaddin will choose.

1126
02:01:17,870 --> 02:01:19,760
I hope he chooses what's best, mother.

1127
02:01:26,640 --> 02:01:29,490
My son will be a warrior!

1128
02:01:29,640 --> 02:01:32,510
He will follow in the footsteps of
his mother and father.

1129
02:01:32,660 --> 02:01:33,660
I hope so.

1130
02:01:33,800 --> 02:01:34,660
Come on.

1131
02:01:36,130 --> 02:01:39,870
His Bala Mother, I want you to pray for
my Orhan.

1132
02:01:41,120 --> 02:01:42,390
Of course!

1133
02:01:42,890 --> 02:01:43,860
Mother.

1134
02:01:48,850 --> 02:01:51,020
Come here, my Orhan.

1135
02:01:51,130 --> 02:01:53,130
In the name of Allah!

1136
02:01:53,710 --> 02:01:55,590
Praise be!

1137
02:02:01,580 --> 02:02:03,570
In the name of Allah!

1138
02:02:04,260 --> 02:02:06,720
May your black mountains never fall.

1139
02:02:07,470 --> 02:02:10,070
May your big tree with a shadow don't
get cut down.

1140
02:02:10,500 --> 02:02:13,640
May your clean water flowing
like blood doesn't dry up.

1141
02:02:14,540 --> 02:02:16,850
May your wings don't get broken.

1142
02:02:17,390 --> 02:02:18,290
Amen.

1143
02:02:18,410 --> 02:02:22,120
May Almighty Allah not make you needy.

1144
02:02:22,530 --> 02:02:25,400
May your horse run like the wind.

1145
02:02:25,520 --> 02:02:29,040
May your sword never get down.

1146
02:02:29,350 --> 02:02:32,330
May you not be harmed while you fight.

1147
02:02:32,570 --> 02:02:35,420
May your hope always last.

1148
02:02:35,960 --> 02:02:37,290
Finally...

1149
02:02:37,420 --> 02:02:40,060
... may you never lose your faith.

1150
02:02:40,750 --> 02:02:44,960
-We made your prayer, may it be accepted.
-Amen!

1151
02:02:45,530 --> 02:02:47,570
May Almighty Allah...

1152
02:02:47,730 --> 02:02:53,750
...forgive all our sins, in the name of
Muhammad.

1153
02:02:54,040 --> 02:02:55,560
Amen!

1154
02:03:02,390 --> 02:03:06,170
May those who say ''Amen!'' to this prayer
see Allah.

1155
02:03:06,380 --> 02:03:08,120
Amen!

1156
02:03:08,670 --> 02:03:10,380
Amen!

1157
02:03:41,130 --> 02:03:43,840
Darkness takes all disguises...

1158
02:03:43,960 --> 02:03:44,790
...Nikola.

1159
02:03:45,120 --> 02:03:47,120
Because it is everywhere.

1160
02:03:48,930 --> 02:03:50,550
What is this preparation for, Sir?

1161
02:03:51,110 --> 02:03:52,820
I received a letter from the pope.

1162
02:03:53,490 --> 02:03:55,400
Argun wants to unite with the papacy...

1163
02:03:55,540 --> 02:03:57,980
...and take Jerusalem from the Muslims.

1164
02:03:59,490 --> 02:04:00,910
I am going to Jerusalem.

1165
02:04:02,200 --> 02:04:03,310
Nikola...

1166
02:04:03,670 --> 02:04:05,460
...you will fight.

1167
02:04:05,780 --> 02:04:07,000
For our cause.

1168
02:04:07,170 --> 02:04:10,310
You will attack Osman with cruelty
he has never seen before.

1169
02:04:11,110 --> 02:04:12,450
I've always fought.

1170
02:04:13,020 --> 02:04:14,420
Still do.

1171
02:04:15,250 --> 02:04:16,580
You weren't here.

1172
02:04:19,770 --> 02:04:21,530
Now you are leaving.

1173
02:04:23,270 --> 02:04:25,090
For Jerusalem, Nikola.

1174
02:04:26,360 --> 02:04:28,040
I trusted you.

1175
02:04:28,760 --> 02:04:30,180
What will I do now?

1176
02:04:30,590 --> 02:04:33,330
I made you the bey of two tribes, Barkın.

1177
02:04:33,470 --> 02:04:34,520
You grew stronger.

1178
02:04:34,890 --> 02:04:38,130
Use this power wisely.

1179
02:04:38,320 --> 02:04:41,440
If I see even a faint light when I return
...

1180
02:04:41,860 --> 02:04:44,170
...I will bury it in my darkness.

1181
02:04:46,190 --> 02:04:47,350
You will...

1182
02:04:47,590 --> 02:04:49,500
...sleep, Barkın.

1183
02:04:51,260 --> 02:04:54,750
You will be with Osman until it is time.

1184
02:04:55,090 --> 02:04:57,920
You will be his friend for our cause.

1185
02:05:31,120 --> 02:05:34,280
I signed the peace treaty they wanted.

1186
02:05:37,200 --> 02:05:38,870
Did you make peace, Osman Bey?

1187
02:05:42,320 --> 02:05:43,500
With Nikola?

1188
02:05:45,520 --> 02:05:48,730
Sultan Mesud and Emperor were together.

1189
02:05:49,540 --> 02:05:51,630
Should've I said no, Turgut Bey?

1190
02:05:54,320 --> 02:05:55,210
But...

1191
02:05:57,540 --> 02:05:59,460
...I got everything I wanted.

1192
02:06:00,530 --> 02:06:02,010
Don't, Osman Bey!

1193
02:06:02,220 --> 02:06:03,320
Don't!

1194
02:06:03,690 --> 02:06:06,480
You can't have given up on conquering
İnegöl, can you?

1195
02:06:07,190 --> 02:06:08,480
I made the deal.

1196
02:06:10,500 --> 02:06:12,680
But you won't stop.

1197
02:06:14,560 --> 02:06:17,040
We will corner İnegöl so bad that...

1198
02:06:17,960 --> 02:06:20,030
...Nikola won't be able to even breathe.

1199
02:06:20,170 --> 02:06:22,170
That's better!

1200
02:06:22,480 --> 02:06:24,140
Thank you, Osman Bey!

1201
02:06:24,360 --> 02:06:26,760
Nikola was already my archenemy.

1202
02:06:26,900 --> 02:06:29,450
I'm gonna hit him for my friend
one more time.

1203
02:06:29,610 --> 02:06:31,140
It's my honor.

1204
02:06:32,070 --> 02:06:34,780
We must put Nikola in such a position
that...

1205
02:06:34,890 --> 02:06:36,680
...he gets slap after slap, Kosses!

1206
02:06:36,840 --> 02:06:39,610
Even his people will prefer Kayı to him.

1207
02:06:40,410 --> 02:06:41,690
Thus...

1208
02:06:42,290 --> 02:06:45,170
...if they don't give me Nikola's mines...

1209
02:06:46,850 --> 02:06:48,970
...I said I wouldn't accept the treaty.

1210
02:06:49,520 --> 02:06:50,780
Thank you!

1211
02:06:55,090 --> 02:06:59,240
Without the mines, Nikola's income
will fall in half.

1212
02:07:00,200 --> 02:07:01,500
It will.

1213
02:07:01,810 --> 02:07:02,980
It will.

1214
02:07:04,880 --> 02:07:06,980
From now on, the mines are property of
Kayı.

1215
02:07:11,470 --> 02:07:12,570
Thank you.

1216
02:07:13,040 --> 02:07:14,820
Let him become very weak...

1217
02:07:15,020 --> 02:07:18,420
... so that when his people
turn their backs on him...

1218
02:07:18,420 --> 02:07:20,870
...he will lose all his strength
and weapons.

1219
02:07:21,860 --> 02:07:24,770
First I cut his connection to İnegöl.

1220
02:07:26,980 --> 02:07:28,160
Now...

1221
02:07:29,800 --> 02:07:32,330
..I'm going to cut his carotid.

1222
02:07:47,670 --> 02:07:49,640
Byzantine's brave sons!

1223
02:07:51,120 --> 02:07:57,610
We have no longer have anything to do with
the coward emperor or the vile lords!

1224
02:07:58,270 --> 02:08:01,190
What will we do now?

1225
02:08:02,250 --> 02:08:06,740
We will ride our horses both to east and
west!

1226
02:08:07,260 --> 02:08:14,020
We will gather all the mercenaries here!
All of them!

1227
02:08:14,320 --> 02:08:20,340
You will bring me Peteleks, Kumans,
Baltalı Barbar Vareks.

1228
02:08:21,290 --> 02:08:27,910
You will bring the Kumans who will cause
Osman to extinct to me!

1229
02:08:28,620 --> 02:08:29,710
Clear?

1230
02:08:29,880 --> 02:08:31,380
Clear, Sir!

1231
02:08:31,470 --> 02:08:34,230
-Clear?
-Clear, Sir!

1232
02:08:36,110 --> 02:08:37,160
Good!

1233
02:08:52,570 --> 02:08:53,560
I will...

1234
02:08:56,090 --> 02:08:58,650
...destroy you, Osman.

1235
02:09:00,930 --> 02:09:03,840
I will destroy you!

1236
02:09:04,980 --> 02:09:07,090
I will destroy you!

1237
02:09:09,310 --> 02:09:11,520
I will cut his head...

1238
02:09:11,780 --> 02:09:13,780
...off his body and...

1239
02:09:13,990 --> 02:09:16,200
...throw it to the Pope's feet!

1240
02:09:16,320 --> 02:09:17,700
I will say, ''Here!''...

1241
02:09:17,840 --> 02:09:20,150
...''Osman Bey is here''

1242
02:09:20,550 --> 02:09:24,860
Since the emperor and the lords left me
alone in this war...

1243
02:09:25,020 --> 02:09:28,830
...I will say that I won this war
on my own!

1244
02:09:28,950 --> 02:09:30,330
On my own!

1245
02:09:31,500 --> 02:09:32,920
No Caesar!

1246
02:09:33,110 --> 02:09:35,520
I will say that I became Caesar!
I did!

1247
02:09:35,650 --> 02:09:37,150
Aya Nikola!

1248
02:09:38,910 --> 02:09:43,740
I will only open one grave for your
seven lineages!

1249
02:09:44,080 --> 02:09:48,980
I will bury women, children, and
old people in a single grave!

1250
02:09:49,070 --> 02:09:52,440
I swear! I swear!

1251
02:09:53,320 --> 02:09:54,830
I will carry...

1252
02:09:55,110 --> 02:10:00,620
...Kosses' head from castle to castle!

1253
02:10:00,870 --> 02:10:04,760
I will carry that Turgut's head, who
trusts himself too much...

1254
02:10:04,760 --> 02:10:07,260
...from tribe to tribe!

1255
02:10:07,410 --> 02:10:10,280
I swear on Caesar that...

1256
02:10:10,730 --> 02:10:15,200
...I, Aya Nikola...

1257
02:10:15,350 --> 02:10:18,180
...will be called for ages!

1258
02:10:18,410 --> 02:10:21,010
Those who wrong Nikola...

1259
02:10:22,360 --> 02:10:26,950
...always pay the price.

1260
02:10:27,190 --> 02:10:29,610
All of you will pay!

1261
02:10:29,730 --> 02:10:32,140
All of you!

1262
02:10:35,650 --> 02:10:40,340
Forgiveness and great reward.

1263
02:10:41,840 --> 02:10:44,080
What a beautiful truth Allah
the zealous told.

1264
02:10:53,210 --> 02:10:55,940
My Almighty Allah.

1265
02:11:00,490 --> 02:11:08,120
For the sake of our Prophet Muhammad...

1266
02:11:10,500 --> 02:11:14,730
...in honor of the most honorable
book you sent him...

1267
02:11:16,420 --> 02:11:24,190
...may you make my feet firm
on the cause of Islam.

1268
02:11:29,830 --> 02:11:30,970
My Allah...

1269
02:11:33,950 --> 02:11:46,970
...I swear by the night, the day, the
throne and your ninety-nine names that...

1270
02:11:47,360 --> 02:11:54,160
Give victory to my sword for
the cause of Islam...

1271
02:11:54,770 --> 02:12:00,180
...which I raised for the cause of Islam.

1272
02:12:07,190 --> 02:12:16,180
The Prophet Ekrem was patient with
infidels in the Hudaybi Agreement.

1273
02:12:16,750 --> 02:12:24,840
His patience opened the doors of Mecca
to our Prophet and his people.

1274
02:12:28,900 --> 02:12:39,560
Those infidels thought our Prophet
would stop.

1275
02:12:41,870 --> 02:12:47,620
But the great Prophet...

1276
02:12:48,040 --> 02:12:51,850
...got even stronger.

1277
02:12:52,250 --> 02:12:54,640
Oh, the one who is generous...

1278
02:12:55,160 --> 02:12:58,160
...my merciful Allah...

1279
02:12:58,650 --> 02:13:07,950
...you are the Rabb of those who stay
patient for theşr cause.

1280
02:13:13,020 --> 02:13:20,180
Until I am granted the conquest of
İnegöl...

1281
02:13:23,310 --> 02:13:27,660
...make time my friend, my Rabb.

1282
02:13:29,590 --> 02:13:30,920
My Allah...

1283
02:13:31,640 --> 02:13:35,400
...keep me on your way.

1284
02:13:36,680 --> 02:13:44,430
My Allah, I have no other purpose than to
spread the light of Islam to the world.

1285
02:13:45,650 --> 02:14:03,430
To wave the banner of Islam all over the
world, choose me ane my lineage, my Allah.

1286
02:14:10,020 --> 02:14:12,370
Amen!

1287
02:14:16,490 --> 02:15:16,600
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com